    {
      "id": "hcxjfgf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Forests of Karnataka"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Karnataka's forest vegetation ranges from tropical evergreen along the Western Ghats to dry deciduous and thorn scrub in the eastern plains.",
        "The state hosts five major National Parks: Bandipur, Nagarhole, Kudremukh, Anshi (Kali), and Bannerghatta.",
        "Part of the Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve falls within Karnataka, acting as an essential corridor for Asian Elephants.",
        "Official State Symbols include the Asian Elephant (Animal), Indian Roller (Bird), Sandalwood (Tree), and Lotus (Flower).",
        "Environmental conservation strategies focus heavily on biodiversity hotspots and protecting endangered species like the Tiger and Lion-tailed Macaque."
      ],
      "id": "q7jn0co"
    },
